 "post": {
  "title": "How Many Folds to Reach the Moon? #shorts",
  "desc": "Paper is 0.1 mm (0.004 in) thick. Each fold doubles it. How many folds until the stack reaches the Moon?\n\nAnswer: 42 folds.\n\n*A thought experiment. In real life, the record is 12 folds (Britney Gallivan, 2002, with a 4,000 ft strip of thin paper).\n*Earth and Moon are enlarged so you can see them.\n\nSources: NASA Moon Facts (average distance 238,855 miles), FAI (Karman line, 100 km), ESA (geostationary orbit, 35,786 km), Guinness World Records.\nSimulation and animation: original.",
